\nooverflow\faroman\ls3\rin0\lin360\itap0 {\b\f1 Automatic Recovery.}{\f1  Things do go wrong sometimes, but you need
 not to worry. MultiContacts registers its every step. If, for any reason, MultiContacts could not exit cleanly - it will recognize the problem and fix it during the next run. You can even "kill" the application to see this feature working!
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20\cf1 \loch\af0\dbch\af0\hich\f0 \'95\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li360\ri0\sa100\sl200\slmult0\widctlpar
