\par }{\b\f1\ul Terms and Definitions:}{\b\f1 
\par Contact List}{\f1  - a database file, which could be used with EPOC\~Contacts application.
\par }{\b\f1 Contacts App}{\f1  - an EPOC\~contacts application.
\par }{\b\f1 Contacts INI\~file}{\f1  - a file where Contacts App stores your preferences for each Contact List. Preferences include the view settings and field selection.
\par }{\b\f1 ShortCut to Contact List}{\f1  - a special file that references }{\i\f1 Contact Lis}{\f1 t and can be use to start Contacts application with respective }{\i\f1 Contact List}{\f1 .
\par }{\b\f1 Broken ShortCut}{\f1  - a ShortCut which refers to the Contact List, that does not exist anymore or was moved from its original location.
\par }{\b\f1 Clean Exit}{\f1  - MultiContacts exists "cleanly" when it does not have any problems copying Contact Lists to their original locations.
\par 
\par }{\b\f1\ul Modes of Operations:}{\f1 
\par }{\b\f1 Full Operation Mode}{\f1 . MultiContacts starts in Full Operation Mode when
 started from the Extras Bar. Full Operation Mode allows creation of Blank Contact Lists and their respective ShortCuts, creation of ShortCuts to the existing Contact Lists, opening of the existing Contact Lists.
\par }{\b\f1 Create Operation Mode}{\f1 . MultiContacts starts in Create Operation Mode when started by the EPOC }{\i\f1 Create New File}{\f1  command (Ctrl+N). In this mode MultiContacts allows to create one blank Contact List and a ShortCut to it.
\par }{\b\f1 ShortCut Operation Mode}{\f1 . MultiContacts starts in ShortCut Operation Mode when started by tapping on the ShortCut to Contact List. In this mode MultiContacts starts EPOC\~Contacts application with the specified Contact List.
\par }{\b\f1 Data Recovery Mode}{\f1 . MultiContacts starts in Data Recovery Mode when it could not exit "cleanly" during the previous
 run (i.e. system crash, application was "killed", etc.). In this Mode MultiContacts will show which steps were executed successfully and propose to recover data automatically. }{\b\f1 EPOC}{\f1 \~}{\b\f1 
Contacts App will be disabled during the Data Recovery Mode even if you chose not to disable Contacts App in the Preferences.
\par 
\par }{\b\f1\ul Broken ShortCuts recovery.}{\b\f1 
\par }{\f1 MultiContacts will prompt you to delete and re-create a Broken ShortCut. ShortCuts are ALWAYS\~created in the same folder with the Contact List. You can copy or move the ShortCut after it is created.
\par 
\par }{\b\f1\ul Manual Data Recovery}{\b\f1 
\par }{\f1 In the unfortunate event of system crash or similar catastrophe, you might choose to Recover your Contact Lists manually.
\par Please note, that your Original (or System) Contact List can be found in }{\f6 C:\\System\\Data}{\f1  folder. File is: }{\f6 Contacts.cdb
\par }{\f1 During execution of MultiContacts, your System Contact List is backed up to }{\f6 C:\\System\\Apps\\MultiContacts\\Contacts.Cdb.Bak}{\f1  file. Your User Contact Lists remain in the Folder where you chose to keep them.
\par Original (or System) Contacts App INI file can be found in }{\f6 C:\\System\\Apps\\Contacts}{\f1  folder. File is: }{\f6 Contacts.ini
\par }{\f1 During execution of MultiContacts, your System Contacts App INI\~file is backed up to }{\f6 C:\\System\\Apps\\MultiContacts\\Contacts.ini.Bak}{\f1  file. 
\par Your User Contact List INI file remains in the folder with the Contact List itself.
\par 
\par 
\par }{\b\f1\ul Execution Steps}{\b\f1 
\par }{\f1 It is very important to understand what Contact List is located where during MultiContacts session. Those are the steps of MultiContacts execution with file locations (assuming you use Contacts App INI\~files):
\par 1. Back Up System Contact List
\par File }{\f6 c:\\system\\data\\contacts.cdb }{\f1 is copied to}{\f6  \line c:\\system\\apps\\multicontacts\\contacts.cdb.bak
\par }{\f1 File }{\f6 c:\\system\\apps\\contacts\\contacts.ini }{\f1 is copied to}{\f6  c:\\system\\apps\\multicontacts\\contacts.ini.bak
\par }{\f1 2. User Contact List is copied to System Contact List
\par File }{\f6 c:\\documents\\contacts\\private.cdb }{\f1 is copied to }{\f6 c:\\system\\data\\contacts.cdb
\par }{\f1 File }{\f6 c:\\documents\\contacts\\private.cdb.ini }{\f1 is copied to }{\f6 c:\\system\\apps\\contacts\\contacts.ini
\par }{\f1 3. Epoc Contacts application is started. MultiContacts waits for Contacts to finish.
\par 4. Epoc Contacts application has finished. MultiContacts did not move any file yet.
\par 5. User Contact List is copied back to Contacts Folder of User's choice. File }{\f6 c:\\system\\data\\contacts.cdb }{\f1 is copied to }{\f6 c:\\documents\\contacts\\private.cdb
\par }{\f1 File }{\f6 c:\\system\\apps\\contacts\\contacts.ini }{\f1 is copied to }{\f6 c:\\documents\\contacts\\private.cdb.ini
\par }{\f1 6. System Contact List Restored
\par File }{\f6 c:\\system\\apps\\multicontacts\\contacts.cdb.bak }{\f1 is copied to }{\f6 c:\\system\\data\\contacts.cdb
